      "invariant": "INV-M9AMAYWY",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Accepts a requested path as an anchor spelling only when PathSeed validation succeeds and the validated value is byte-identical to the request. A padded or otherwise normalized spelling returns False and is never matched to the path it would normalize to.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "bc638f5e47c02721604a66086ebc28876ec93f4c",
        "content": "sha256:9bf4e1e3d753bd5a6fd2070b32e9c81f1ada34a122b0a1a82f7981ab2e12b42b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_bound_knowledge"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-7GKF4ASW",
      "invariant": "INV-RS0EVBHD",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Chooses which knowledge may admit an unchanged path. The resolution's own halves are used when the requested after tree is the one the leaf binds now; otherwise it searches this leaf's comparison generations from newest to oldest for one that recorded exactly the requested tree pair and reopens it. With no such generation it returns an explicit no-knowledge link, and the leaf's current knowledge is never substituted.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "bc638f5e47c02721604a66086ebc28876ec93f4c",
        "content": "sha256:f17f1fac35685d723b396fe3ab0f16850dad7d409ed3c9f8215e03adc5bbf52f",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_side_reading"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-CHBR2MK5",
      "invariant": "INV-XTXZESS6",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Asks one bound snapshot through the read owner's exact fetch_realizations_at_path query, which reads claims at one path and expands no family, so scope size cannot fail it. When that finds no realization it asks the snapshot's derived index for a proof entry at the path, which only a tree comparison's index holds, and reads a proof as linked too. An absent snapshot is reported as unread and marked absent, an unreadable one as unread with its cause, never as not_linked.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "bc638f5e47c02721604a66086ebc28876ec93f4c",
        "content": "sha256:7ca3162b210e28ae0b41ff020882d0b9ec231cc4ff6de3e8094ac12962e5256b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "recorded_realization_link"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-HD60BGRJ",
      "invariant": "INV-9ECAFVTQ",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Answers whether the requested comparison's own knowledge links the path. It uses only the knowledge bound to that comparison (_bound_knowledge), requires the exact spelling to be anchor-shaped with no nearby match, reads each half for an anchor at exactly that path, and reports the linking sides; the result is undetermined when a half could not be read.",
      "role": "support"
    }
  ],
